"""Record the actual subsequent reread of the retained original Colmez proof."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv,datetime,hashlib,json
w=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
src=w/'agents/reduction_descent/sources/colmez_corps_locaux.txt'
now=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()
r={'actual_utc':now,'status':'PASS: original proof reread',
 'source':'Pierre Colmez, Corps locaux, retained original PDF text',
 'retained_text':str(src.relative_to(w)),
 'retained_text_sha256':hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),
 'actual_read_scope':'Remark3.6, complete Proposition3.7 proof, Lemma3.8 and Corollary3.9 proofs, full Theorem3.10 proof, and full Proposition3.13 proof; printed pp14--16.',
 'own_check':'For an actual normal quotient, the norm polynomial shows equality of the ideals generated by the quotient uniformizer displacement and the product of all lift displacements. Normalized valuations give the exact coset average for i=b+1. The piecewise-linear identity averages min(i,u+1), and the maximal lift displacement converts that identity to Herbrand quotient compatibility. Inverting the compositional identity gives Proposition3.13(ii), upper numbering passing to the actual quotient. Lower numbering restricts directly because the uniformizer on the common top field is unchanged.',
 'wording_correction':'Theorem3.10 is not a proposition; the canonical B90 citation should identify Proposition3.7, Theorem3.10 and Proposition3.13(ii).',
 'printed_variable_slip':'In the derivative paragraph of Theorem3.10(ii), the intermediate argument v must be phi_(L/K)(u), as demanded by differentiating phi_(K/F) composed with phi_(L/K); the displayed product and our proof use this correctly. No result is inferred from the mistyped intermediate subscript.',
 'relation_to_prior_audit':'This is an additional actual reread after outputs/root_B90_audit.json was recorded, not a redating or alteration of that completed audit.'}
